<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Anthropic report: Is Russia using AI for disinformation in the Central African Republic and elsewhere?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:735d473d877d87701f83407f108df0e63df8216b7eccc8c86cc6e55571ca4725</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T17:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-report-is-russia-using-ai-for-disinformation-in-the-central-african-republic-and-elsewhere/a-79476947--5ab896d891c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-report-is-russia-using-ai-for-disinformation-in-the-central-african-republic-and-elsewhere/a-79476947?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An Anthropic report says the AI model Claude was used in pro-Russian campaigns in the Central African Republic. Similar allegations were raised for the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Sudan and Mali.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>In Tigray, Ethiopian government forces have advanced against a northern rebel group, reports indicate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63e76dcc4f6526a255eeaa7962375034ad0a057f57c89e580ae243fd22578803</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T03:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-tigray-ethiopian-government-forces-have-advanced-against-a-northern-rebel-group-reports-indicate/a-79534372--ed90e271ae47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-tigray-ethiopian-government-forces-have-advanced-against-a-northern-rebel-group-reports-indicate/a-79534372?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reports indicate Ethiopian government forces have made advances against a northern rebel group. Renewed fighting has raised fears the conflict could spill over into the wider region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's first female head of government: Symbol or real reform?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:696bee2c524dcb5f8433da2441c55109e255a63e7f2f43ec1c863fd4a94b5790</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808--5c6131d5d637.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatima Zahra Mansouri has been chosen as Morocco's first female prime minister. Is her appointment a kind of symbolism, to show Morocco in a positive light? Or could Mansouri bring genuine changes for Moroccan women?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Growing fear of war in the Horn of Africa after Eritrea cuts ties with Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa20e4c9374cacfbef413eeb88c42e205df55bea94ec9abbe4ef8d67912ede1e</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/growing-fear-of-war-in-the-horn-of-africa-after-eritrea-cuts-ties-with-ethiopia/a-79513311--226a98e4fbfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/growing-fear-of-war-in-the-horn-of-africa-after-eritrea-cuts-ties-with-ethiopia/a-79513311?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Tigray conflict is no longer just a domestic issue. As Ethiopia, Eritrea and Egypt trade accusations, the African Union (AU) urges restraint. Is the Horn of Africa hurtling toward a wider regional crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13c0e28f170b521025d902385c1de7834ff75decd575ef6505bf0df146298e65</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:169984085d644b89ea72d29c527dc0b42f092b0b5ec517d9d68894c908f078f5</id><updated>2026-10-04T19:43:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
